title: The Right calls a constructive vote of no confidence against the current government!
subtitle: We have angered our coalition partners too much...
new-page: true
on-arrival: tried_supporting_kpd = 0; z_relation -= 5 if not in_social_catholic_coalition; dvp_relation -= 5 if in_grand_coalition; ddp_relation -= 5 if not in_social_catholic_coalition; lvp_relation -= 5 if in_weimar_coalition and not in_social_catholic_coalition or in_grand_coalition; lvp_right += 2 if in_weimar_coalition or in_grand_coalition; dvp_right += 2 if in_grand_coalition; ddp_right += 1; hindenburg_angry += 20
on-departure: secularized = 0
view-if: chancellor_party == "SPD" and spd_in_government = 1 and ((in_grand_coalition = 1 or in_popular_front = 1 or in_minority_government = 1 or (in_social_catholic_coalition and cvp_formed) and (z_coalition_dissent >= 3 or (not lvp_exists and dvp_exists and dvp_coalition_dissent >= 3) or (lvp_exists and lvp_coalition_dissent >= 3)) or (in_weimar_coalition = 1 and not (in_social_catholic_coalition and cvp_formed) and ((z_coalition_dissent >= 4) or (not lvp_exists and ddp_coalition_dissent >= 4) or (lvp_exists and lvp_coalition_dissent >= 4)) and spd_r < 50 and constructive_vonc and ((bourgeois_coalition >= 50) or (dnvp_ideology == "Moderate" and center_right_coalition >= 50 and dnf_formed and not (year = 1929 and month >= 7)) or (right_coalition >= 50 and (dnvp_ideology == "Moderate" or dnvp_westarp) and not (year = 1929 and month >= 7)))
tags: event
go-to: vonc_menu

= Constructive Vote of No Confidence

The [? if z_party_name != "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">Center Party</span>?][? if z_party_name == "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">**CVP**</span>?] has called for a constructive vote of no confidence against us, due to our various policies and disagreements. If this succeeds, a new government will be formed under Heinrich Brüning.

@vonc_menu

- @try_assuage: Try to assuage our partners.
- @right_coalition: Brüning forms a right-wing coalition.
- @center_right_coalition: Brüning forms a center-right coalition.
- @bourgeois_coalition: Brüning forms a bourgeois coalition.
- @snap_elections: President [+ president +] will call snap elections.

@try_assuage

How do we assuage our partners?

- @dvp_prussia_2: Let the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> into Prussia.
- @give_up_prussia: Give up on leadership of Prussia.
- @austerity: Enact a massive austerity plan.
- @resources: Use our resources to reduce dissent within the coalition.
- @vonc_menu: Never mind. What are our options?

@dvp_prussia_2
view-if: year <= 1929 and in_grand_coalition_prussia = 0 and (in_weimar_coalition_prussia or in_minority_weimar_coalition_prussia) and in_grand_coalition = 1 and dvp_was_in_prussia == 0 and not lvp_formed
choose-if: z_leader != "Kaas" and not secularized
unavailable-subtitle: [? if z_leader = "Kaas": Kaas and the [? if z_party_name != "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">Center</span>?][? if z_party_name == "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">**CVP**</span>?] strongly dissents against. ?]
on-arrival: in_right_coalition_prussia = 0; in_weimar_coalition_prussia = 0; in_grand_coalition_prussia = 1; in_minority_grand_coalition_prussia = 0; in_popular_front_prussia = 0; in_left_front_prussia = 0; sapd_toleration_prussia = 0; in_spd_majority_prussia = 0; in_center_right_coalition_prussia = 0; in_far_right_coalition_prussia = 0; in_minority_weimar_coalition_prussia = 0; ddp_in_popular_front_prussia = 0; kpd_goals_seen_prussia = 0; spd_toleration_prussia = 0; dvp_relation += 10; z_relation -= 5; ddp_relation += 3; z_coalition_dissent -= 1; dvp_coalition_dissent -= 1; ddp_coalition_dissent -= 1; lvp_coalition_dissent -= 1; left_dissent += 5; in_grand_coalition_prussia = 1; dvp_left += 3; new_middle_dvp += 3

Letting the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> into the Prussian government is an offer too good for them to refuse, no matter their leadership. 

However, this has negatively impacted our freedom of action we previously had in the <span style="color: #000000;">We</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">im</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ar</span> coalition.

@give_up_prussia
subtitle: Braun would need to resign.
view-if: prussia_leader = "Braun" and neo_weimar_coalition_prussia >= 50
on-arrival: z_coalition_dissent = 1 if z_coalition_dissent > 1; ddp_coalition_dissent = 1 if ddp_coalition_dissent > 1; dvp_coalition_dissent = 1 if dvp_coalition_dissent > 1; lvp_coalition_dissent = 1 if lvp_coalition_dissent > 1; ; prussia_leader = "Stegerwald"; prussia_leader = "Brüning" if z_leader == "Stegerwald"; reformist_dissent += 10; center_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 10; left_dissent += 5; workers_spd -= 5; new_middle_spd -= 5; rural_spd -= 3; braun_resign = 1

Fine. We no longer control the government of Prussia. The vote has been called off.

The Minister-President position is transferred to the [? if z_party_name != "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">Center</span>?][? if z_party_name == "CVP": <span style="color: #000000;">**CVP**</span>?].

@austerity
view-if: welfare >= 0 and not secularized
on-arrival: z_coalition_dissent = 0; ddp_coalition_dissent = 0; dvp_coalition_dissent = 0; lvp_coalition_dissent = 0; workers_spd -= 10; unemployed_spd -= 10; workers_kpd += 7; workers_nsdap += 3; unemployed_kpd += 5; unemployed_nsdap += 5; left_dissent += 15; center_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 15; reformist_dissent += 5; welfare -= 2; budget += 1; unemployed += 3; kpd_coalition_dissent += 1; kpd_relation -= 10 if in_popular_front; goal_spd_cancel += 1; social_welfare_timer = 10

Fine. We enacted a massive austerity program to cut welfare, in order to maintain the stability of our coalition. The vote has been called off.

@resources
view-if: secularized = 0
choose-if: (resources >= 3 and in_weimar_coalition or in_popular_front or in_minority_government) or ((resources >= 3 and in_grand_coalition and not (dvp_ideology == "Right" and year >= 1930) and not lvp_formed) or (resources >= 3 and (in_grand_coalition or in_weimar_coalition) and not (lvp_ideology == "Right" and year >= 1930) and lvp_formed))
unavailable-subtitle: [? if resources < 3: We do not have enough resources. ?] [? if in_grand_coalition and (dvp_ideology == "Right" and year >= 1930) and not lvp_formed: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> doesn't want our resources anymore. ?] [? if (in_grand_coalition or in_weimar_coalition) and (lvp_ideology == "Right" and year >= 1930) and lvp_formed: The <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span> doesn't want our resources anymore. ?]
subtitle: -3 resources
on-arrival: resources -= 3; z_coalition_dissent -= 1 if z_coalition_dissent > 0; ddp_coalition_dissent -= 1 if ddp_coalition_dissent > 0; dvp_coalition_dissent -= 1 if dvp_coalition_dissent > 0; lvp_coalition_dissent -= 1 if lvp_coalition_dissent > 0;

By transferring resources to our coalition partners, we can reduce their dissent against our policies. This is a crude, but effective solution.

@right_coalition
view-if: right_coalition >= 50 and (dnvp_ideology == "Moderate" or dnvp_westarp) and not (year = 1929 and month >= 7)
on-arrival: center_dissent += 5; reformist_dissent += 5; spd_in_government = 0; grand_coalition_collapsed = 1 if in_grand_coalition; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; z_coalition_dissent = 0; ddp_coalition_dissent = 0; dvp_coalition_dissent = 0; lvp_coalition_dissent = 0;
go-to: election_1928.right_coalition_2

@center_right_coalition
view-if: dnvp_ideology == "Moderate" and not lvp_formed and center_right_coalition >= 50 and dnf_formed and right_coalition < 50 and not (year = 1929 and month >= 7)
on-arrival: center_dissent += 5; reformist_dissent += 5; spd_in_government = 0; grand_coalition_collapsed = 1 if in_grand_coalition; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; z_coalition_dissent = 0; ddp_coalition_dissent = 0; dvp_coalition_dissent = 0; lvp_coalition_dissent = 0;
go-to: election_1928.center_right_coalition_2

@bourgeois_coalition
view-if: bourgeois_coalition >= 50 and not cvp_formed
on-arrival: spd_in_government = 0; grand_coalition_collapsed = 1 if in_grand_coalition; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; z_coalition_dissent = 0; ddp_coalition_dissent = 0; dvp_coalition_dissent = 0; lvp_coalition_dissent = 0;
go-to: election_1928.bourgeois_coalition

@snap_elections
view-if: president_ideology == "Left"
choose-if: presidential_powers != 1
unavailable-subtitle: We don't have that power anymore. You really screwed us here with your reforms, you know that?
call: set_next_election_time
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; spd_in_government = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; in_popular_front = 0; spd_toleration = 0; spd_toleration_right = 0; z_coalition_dissent = 0; ddp_coalition_dissent = 0; dvp_coalition_dissent = 0; lvp_coalition_dissent = 0; pro_republic -= 5; old_middle_spd -= 3; new_middle_spd -= 2; workers_spd -= 3 if pro_republic < 50; workers_spd -= 4 if pro_republic < 40; old_middle_nsdap += 4 if pro_republic < 50; new_middle_nsdap += 3 if pro_republic < 50; lvp_right += 3; ddp_right += 2; ddp_cohesion -= 1; dvp_right += 3

To prevent being relegated to the opposition, we have called for new elections for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].
